  "exp": "A data warehouse is defined precisely this way: a subject-oriented, integrated repository that consolidates highly structured, cleaned data pulled from multiple source systems, retained over time for historical trend analysis and reporting. A Data lake (C) is the near-opposite -- it stores raw, often unstructured or semi-structured data without imposing structure upfront. A Database (D) is a single operational system for current transactional data, not an integration point for multiple historical sources. 'Databank' (A) is an informal, non-technical term not used precisely in DBMS theory.",
