  "exp": "In several software testing textbooks, Six Sigma's initial diagnostic phase is summarized as three core steps -- Define (the problem/goal), Measure (current performance data), and Analyze (root causes) -- before the later improvement phases are added. The full standard DMAIC cycle actually has five phases (Define, Measure, Analyze, Improve, Control), but among the four given options only 'define, measure, analyze' forms a coherent, sequential subset matching how the method is introduced; the other options mix phases out of their logical order or omit Define entirely.",
