  "model": "SIGNATURE has 9 letters — S, I, G, N, A, T, U, R, E — and every letter is distinct, so no division for repeated letters is needed anywhere in this problem.\n\nVowels: I, A, U, E (4 of them). Consonants: S, G, N, T, R (5 of them).\n\nThe condition \"vowels always come together\" is handled by the grouping (or \"string\") method: tie the four vowels into one composite letter [IAUE] and treat it as a single object. The arrangement is then over 5 consonants + 1 block = 6 objects, which can be ordered in 6! = 720 ways. Independently, the four vowels inside the block can be permuted among themselves in 4! = 24 ways.\n\nBy the product rule:\n\nRequired number of words = 6! × 4! = 720 × 24 = 17280.\n\nCross-check: total unrestricted arrangements are 9! = 362880, so the vowels-together words are 17280/362880 = 1/21 of all arrangements — the standard result 4!·6!/9!. (\"Words\" here means arrangements of letters, meaningful or not.)",
