  "model": "The word \"only\" fixes the language as the singleton L = {1010} over Σ = {0, 1} — the machine accepts that one string and rejects every other string, including 0, 1, 101, 10101 and 10100. (If the intent had been \"ends with 1010\" or \"contains 1010\" the automaton would differ; the reading taken here is the literal one.)\n\nBecause a DFA must be complete — exactly one transition per state per input symbol — any symbol that departs from the pattern 1-0-1-0, and any symbol after the fourth, must lead to a dead (trap/reject) state qd from which there is no escape. That trap state is unavoidable, not optional.\n\nStates: q0 start, q1, q2, q3, q4 final, qd trap.\n\nTransition table (* marks the final state):\n\n  State |  0   |  1\n  ->q0  |  qd  |  q1\n    q1  |  q2  |  qd\n    q2  |  qd  |  q3\n    q3  |  q4  |  qd\n   *q4  |  qd  |  qd\n    qd  |  qd  |  qd\n\nTrace of 1010: q0 -1-> q1 -0-> q2 -1-> q3 -0-> q4, which is final, so the string is accepted. This 6-state DFA is minimal for {1010}.",
