  "sub": "Percentage, ratio and proportion",
  "q": "The ratio of the number of boys and that of girls in a school having 504 students is 13:11. What will be the new ratio if 3 more girls are admitted?",
  "opts": {
   "A": "6 : 7",
   "B": "10 : 11",
   "C": "11 : 10",
   "D": "7 : 6"
  },
  "ans": "D",
  "exp": "13 + 11 = 24 parts, so 504 students give 21 per part: 273 boys and 231 girls. Three more girls make 234, and 273 : 234 divides by 39 to give 7 : 6.",
  "conf": "official",
  "prov": "Jr. Grade of MES, P&E Cadre (Electrical Wing) under P&E Department and Assistant Architect (Contract) under PWD, July 2023, General Studies, Q80; answer from MPSC's official Final Answer Key dated 8 September 2023 (no provisional key was published for this sitting)",
