  "unit": "6",
  "sub": "Nuclear and defence technology",
  "q": "A moderator is used in nuclear reactors in order to",
  "opts": {
   "A": "decrease the number of neutrons",
   "B": "increase the number of neutrons",
   "C": "speed up the neutrons",
   "D": "slow down the speed of neutrons"
  },
  "ans": "D",
  "exp": "To slow the neutrons down. Fast neutrons released by fission are poor at causing further fission in uranium-235; a moderator such as heavy water or graphite slows them to thermal speeds and sustains the chain reaction. It does not change how many neutrons there are.",
  "conf": "official",
  "prov": "Jr. Grade of MES, P&E Cadre (Electrical Wing) under P&E Department and Assistant Architect (Contract) under PWD, July 2023, General Studies, Q94; answer from MPSC's official Final Answer Key dated 8 September 2023 (no provisional key was published for this sitting)",
